! mcp_bootstrap_p192.strap -- MCP printed page 192: the tail of the
! backspace (BSP) command, the "test for end of SEOP I/O with error
! returns" routine, and the first card of the new-tape routine.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.199.  The header was READ, not
! assumed, at 300 and 600 dpi:  "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID LG000164   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  192".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD READS 221515. <<<
! Six digits, printed after the word LOCATION at the right-hand end of
! the heading line, clear of the dashed rule.  That is LINE 1'S
! location word (docs/transcription_workflow.md step 1), and line 1
! here IS a located row -- the case the rule predicts to be NUMBERED
! rather than blank.  Line 1's own LOCATION column reads 221515.00.
! Two independent witnesses for the origin; see THE JOIN.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIFTY-ONE PRINTED LINES.  THIRTY-TWO COMPILE, EIGHTEEN ARE
! COMMENT CARDS (lines 16-26 and 44-50, printed "--" in the NAME
! column), AND ONE -- line 14's CNOP -- IS A STATEMENT THAT EMITS
! NOTHING, so it is neither.  No SLC, no SYN, no VF, no
! DD, NO RESERVATION OF ANY KIND.  The page is CONTIGUOUS from
! 221515.00 to 221541.77 -- no hole, nothing skipped -- and then
! blank paper to the foot of the form.
!
!   lines  1-15   the tail of the backspace arm: the reject exit
!                 (SIC,KKRET / B,KIOREJ), the four-way return fan
!                 JBSPX (EPGK / UK / EE / normal), the UK-alone
!                 retry through JBSPE, the error-control exit
!                 (SIC,SDISIC / B,SDISP) and JBSPC, the
!                 CTL(SEOP) card that issues control code 0o176.
!   lines 16-26   the banner and calling sequence for what follows:
!                 "***** TEST FOR END OF SEOP I/O WITH ERROR
!                 RETURNS *****", then LINKAGE....LVI,$1,$+1.0 /
!                 B,JSEOPT with the four returns documented as bits
!                 60, 61, 62 of $R (EOP in bit 63).
!   lines 27-43   J SEOP T itself: LCI,14,K REP sets the retry
!                 count, CCW copies the channel control word into
!                 JKCCW, BZEKJZ tests the EKJ indicator, CB counts
!                 down to JSEOPT+.32, and JSEOPZ loops on the SEOP
!                 bit (BB,JKCCW+.24) until the I/O is done; then
!                 L(BU,4),JKCCW+.19 pulls the EPGK/UK/EE/EOP bits
!                 and the three BB/B cards fan out on them.  Line
!                 43 is JKCCW, the copied control word.
!   lines 44-51   "***** TRY TO GET A NEW TAPE *****", its linkage
!                 comment, and JNEWTE -- the one compiled card,
!                 TI,3,$1,JNEWXR.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SPAN, ESTABLISHED FROM THE PAGE (NOT FROM THE SURVEY)
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The brief no longer quotes survey endpoints and this deck did not
! consult them.  The span was established three ways and they agree:
!
!   * THE LINE COLUMN runs 1..51 with no break.  Line 1 is located
!     (221515.00); line 51 is located (221541.00); nothing is
!     printed below line 51 but the closing dashed rule.
!   * THE CARD-SERIAL COLUMN runs LG000164 (line 1, and the
!     heading's own "CARD ID" says LG000164 too) to LG000213 (line
!     51), fifty serials for fifty-one lines.  There is exactly one
!     duplicate, LG000195 on lines 32 AND 33, which is the
!     SIC/branch pair "SIC,SDISIC ; B,SDISP" punched on one card --
!     the "one card, one WORD" shape printed p.184 recorded.  No
!     gap at either end, so nothing fell off.
!     (Note that lines 12/13 are the SAME two statements on TWO
!     cards, LG000175 and LG000176.  So one-card-per-word is a
!     habit of the punch, not a rule of the assembler.)
!   * THE COUNTER CHAIN closes digit for digit from 221515.00 to
!     221541.77 with every intermediate location printed on the
!     page and no gap between any two of them.  Assembled, the deck
!     occupies 0o221515..0o221541 -- TWENTY-ONE WORDS, printed, and
!     a hole-scan over that range reports NONE.  Thirty-two
!     compiled rows: TWENTY-TWO half-word instructions, NINE
!     full-word instructions and ONE CW, which is 22/2 + 9 + 1 =
!     21 words exactly -- the span, with no slack.  Line 14's
!     CNOP emits nothing because the counter is already on a word
!     boundary when it is reached, which is why it prints no
!     location.
!
! THE SECOND, MACHINE READING (workflow step 2a).
! `python3 strap/mcp_ocr.py 192` reads SIXTEEN of the thirty-two
! located rows cleanly and agrees with the eye on FIFTEEN.  The one
! disagreement is line 15: tesseract says 221524.60, the eye says
! 221524.00.  The eye wins and it is not close -- .60 is not a
! half-word boundary, line 13 is a half word at 221523.40 so the
! counter stands at 221524.00, and line 27 prints 221525.00 one
! full word later.  Recorded because a disagreement found and
! settled is worth more than sixteen silent agreements.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN, BOTH WAYS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! BACKWARD.  >>> THIS DECK'S SLC IS NOT PRINTED. <<<  The page
! carries no SLC card at all, so the origin 221515.00 is ASSERTED,
! not checked.  Its two witnesses are both on this page and both
! independent of my reading of the statements:
!
!   * the heading row's own LOCATION field, "221515", printed by
!     IBM's assembler;
!   * line 1's own LOCATION column, 221515.00.
!
! >>> AND IT IS ASSERTED RATHER THAN CHECKED, MEASURED. <<<  The
! workflow's way out (a landed deck that SYNs a label this page
! DEFINES makes the origin CHECKED by the merge) does not apply:
! grepped over all of decks/, NO landed deck mentions JBSPX, JBSPC,
! JSEOPT, JSEOPZ, JKCCW or JNEWTE.  The injection was run anyway --
! origin shifted one half word to (8)221515.40 and the body image
! re-merged -- and it was ACCEPTED (772 defined, 71 external, the
! same numbers as the unshifted merge), which is the measurement
! that says "asserted".  See JOINING IT TO THE BODY IMAGE below.
!
! >>> BUT THE VOLUME OCR OF printed p.191 CORROBORATES IT, AND IT
! >>> IS A DIFFERENT PAGE, WHICH IS THE ONE THING THE VOLUME OCR
! >>> IS GOOD FOR. <<<  docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt's PDF p.198
! block ends:
!
!   [p191 l.37]  221512.40  221512.44 44  K K RET BZCBJZ,$ -RETURN
!   [p191 l.44]  (comment)   --   LINKAGE ,SIC,JBSPX
!   [p191 l.45]  (comment)   --           B,JBSPE
!   [p191 l.48]  221514.40  221524.00 10   <op>  -BSP COMMAND
!
! The last LOCATED row the OCR reads there is line 48 at
! 221514.40, and it compiles a SINGLE half word, so the counter
! arriving at this page is 221515.00 -- this page's origin, read
! off another page's ink.
!
! TWO CAVEATS, both of which an earlier draft of this note got
! wrong and both of which matter:
!   * I DO NOT NAME THE MNEMONIC on that row.  The OCR reads
!     "LX #0,JHSPC" and I cannot identify an operation whose byte
!     is 10 with an octal field of .00 (printed p.184's landed LV
!     rows print 30 and its LVI rows 01).  What corroborates
!     JBSPC is the ADDRESS 221524.00, and that holds whatever the
!     operation turns out to be.
!   * "THE LAST ROW THE OCR READ" IS NOT "THE LAST ROW".  See
!     prediction (7).
! Flagged as a cross-check and not as settled: p.191's deck does
! not exist yet and the reading above is an OCR, not a rendering.
! Three more things fall out of that same block and they are used
! below: K K RET is DEFINED there at 221512.40, K IO REJ is
! DEFINED there at 221505.00 (its line 21), and 221514.40's
! neighbour at 221514.00 is almost certainly JBSPE's defining card
! -- see WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE (B).
!
! FORWARD.  >>> THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 221542.00. <<<
! Line 51 is at 221541.00 and prints TWO half-word groups
! ("000021.00 80  221617.06 A0"), so TI is a FULL WORD at a
! word-aligned location.  221541.00 + 1 word = 221542.00.  This
! does not depend on the one byte this page cost two renders to
! read (A0 vs AC): I2 changes the byte, never the width.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> FALSIFIABLE PREDICTIONS FOR printed p.193 (PDF p.200) <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   (1) >>> ITS FIRST LOCATED ROW IS 221542.00. <<<  Not .40 -- the
!       TI on line 51 is a full word and lands this page's counter
!       on a word boundary.  If p.193's first location is 221541.40
!       or 221542.40, one of us is wrong and it is probably my
!       reading of line 51 as a full word.
!   (2) Its first card serial is LG000214.  WEAKER THAN (1): the
!       brief records two measured cases of a serial printing no
!       listing line (ED000049, IH000041), both at page breaks,
!       which is exactly here.  A missing LG000214 would not
!       falsify the join; a serial BELOW LG000214 would.
!   (3) Its heading-row LOCATION field is NUMBERED, reading
!       221542, UNLESS its line 1 is a banner or comment card, in
!       which case it is blank (printed p.147's case).  I cannot
!       tell which from here.
!   (4) p.193 DEFINES J GETOF at 221546.40.  This is NOT my
!       reading: printed p.184's landed deck SYNs JGETOF at
!       (8)221546.40 and cites the volume OCR of p.193 line 7,
!       "J GETOF CM0000(BU,1),S CK OP($10)".  That is an OCR of
!       ANOTHER page used as an index, which is the one thing the
!       workflow says the volume OCR is good for.  It CORROBORATES
!       prediction (1): 221542.00 .. 221546.40 is four and a half
!       words, which is a plausible six-line run.
!   (5) p.193 does NOT define JNEWXR.  The volume OCR carries its
!       defining card, a THREE-WORD reservation at 221617.00, on
!       a page well past p.193 if (4) holds.
!   (6) p.193 defines none of this page's six labels.
!
! >>> AND ONE BACKWARD, FOR printed p.191 (PDF p.198) <<<
!   (7) p.191 contains a LOCATED row at 221514.40 compiling a
!       SINGLE HALF WORD (printed "221524.00 10", and its address
!       is this page's JBSPC).  That row is p.191's LAST LOCATED
!       row, so any lines after it compile nothing -- because
!       221515.00 is this page's.
!       >>> STATED THAT WAY ON PURPOSE. <<<  The evidence is that
!       the volume OCR's p.191 block ENDS at line 48, and "the
!       last line the OCR read" is not "the last line": the same
!       OCR reads only 16 of this page's 32 located rows, and the
!       brief records it giving up on printed p.181 at line 42.
!       An earlier draft of this note claimed p.191 has no line
!       49 and that claim was not mine to make.
!   (8) p.191 DEFINES a label at 221514.00 which this page spells
!       JBSPE, and the comment cards at its lines 44/45 document
!       the entry pair SIC,JBSPX / B,JBSPE.
!   (9) p.191's last card serial is LG000163.  Same weakness as
!       (2): a serial that prints no line occurs at page breaks.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every line number carries the ordinary trailing asterisk.
! TWO ROWS CARRY A SECOND ASTERISK AFTER THE LOCATION:
!
!     line 13   221523.40 *   B,SDISP
!     line 41   221536.40 *   BB,$R+.61,.32($1)
!
! Recorded, and NO RULE PROPOSED -- and this page is unusual in
! that it REFUTES a statement-shaped rule FROM ITS OWN INK, which
! is the thing the brief says a single page normally cannot do:
!
!     line 13 is "B,SDISP" at 221523.40 and CARRIES the mark;
!     line 33 is "B,SDISP" at 221530.40 and carries NONE.
!
! Same statement, same page, same drum, one marked and one not.
! Likewise neither "SIC,SDISIC" row (12, 32) is marked, and of the
! three BB rows only line 41 is.  So the mark is demonstrably not a
! function of the statement text.  It is also not "every named
! row" (JBSPX, JBSPC, J SEOP T, JSEOPZ, JKCCW, JNEWTE all carry
! none) and not "every full word" (lines 9, 15, 28, 34, 35, 39, 40,
! 51 carry none while 41 does).  Nine things it is not, now.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPH CALLS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (0) >>> NO BLANKET "ROUND GLYPH IS A DAMAGED 0" RULE WAS APPLIED
!     ON THIS PAGE, and the page itself shows why one would be
!     wrong: line 36's byte really is C3 and line 29's really is
!     44, while lines 3, 11, 31 and 42 really are 01.  Shape did
!     not decide any of them.
!
! (1) THE BYTE ON LINES 3, 11, 31 AND 42 IS "01", NOT "C1".  All
!     four print a round glyph in the high nibble.  Settled on what
!     PRODUCED it, twice over and never by shape:
!       * printed p.184's LANDED deck carries four LVI rows and
!         every one prints the byte 01 ("222001.13 01",
!         "222011.17 01", "000011.17 01", "221237.03 01").  Same
!         assembler, different page, different drum impression.
!       * the arithmetic closes: an LVI's printed 6-bit field is
!         2J+1 (p.184's deck states the rule and this page obeys
!         it four times -- $1 -> .03, $14 -> .35 twice), so the
!         index is NOT in the byte and the byte is the bare
!         opcode.  A "C1" would have to mean index 1 on a card
!         whose index is already accounted for.
!     Line 42's "B,1.0($1)" is the same glyph and the same answer:
!     B's byte is 00 unindexed (p.184 line 1) and 01 indexed by $1.
!
! (2) THE OCTAL FIELDS ON THIS PAGE DROP INK CONSTANTLY and that
!     is the rung-5 calibration, nothing more.  Lines 3 and 29
!     print their location-bit fields as ".C3" where only ".03" is
!     possible; lines 7, 15, 28, 40, 41, 43 print "C0C000" and
!     "COCC11" for 000000 and 000011; line 51 prints "COCC21.CO"
!     and "221617.C6".  Per the workflow this licenses nothing
!     about any particular glyph -- it only says the drum CAN open
!     a round character on this page, which is why (1) was settled
!     on the arithmetic instead.
!
! (3) "SEOP" (lines 15, 18, 27, 34 and the labels JSEOPT/JSEOPZ) is
!     SEOP and not SECP.  Not a shape call: SEOP is the Suppress
!     End-Of-Operation modifier of the I-O instructions, and
!     strap_asm's own IO_OP table carries CTLSEOP with the code
!     .15 that line 15 prints ("000176.15 00").  The Reference
!     Manual's control-code table and C28-6129 are the sources
!     strap_asm cites for it.
!
! (4) "BZEKJZ" (line 29) was read at 1200 dpi and is six letters,
!     B-Z-E-K-J-Z, with no blank.  It is a branch-on-indicator:
!     EKJ is indicator 6 in strap_asm's INDICATOR_BITS, the
!     leading Z is the branch-on-ZERO form and the trailing Z
!     resets the indicator.  TWO independent confirmations:
!       * the volume OCR of a DIFFERENT page prints the same
!         mnemonic -- "221266.00  221267.43 44  BZEKJZ,$+1.32" --
!         with the same byte 44 this page prints;
!       * strap_asm assembles BZEKJZ to byte 44 and the whole
!         half word matches.
!     The nearby "BZUNRJZ" and "BZCBJZ" in that same OCR run are
!     the same family and make the spelling a pattern, not a
!     one-off.
!
! (5) "SDISIC" and "SDISP" (lines 12/13 and 32/33) print CLOSED UP
!     on this page.  The volume OCR of the page that DEFINES the
!     caller prints the same two cards one after another at
!     221274.40 and 221275.00, with the same two half words this
!     page prints ("217451.40 80" and "217372.10 00"), spelled
!     with the blank in: "S DISIC" and "S DISP".  Both symbols are
!     already landed in decks/ at exactly these addresses
!     (SDISIC at 217451.40 on pp.103/119/169/173; SDISP at
!     217372.0), so the spelling is settled by the corpus and not
!     by me.
!
! (6) "KCBJR" (line 37) is spelled with a C, not an O.  This is
!     printed p.184's GLYPH CALL (8) and it was settled there
!     twice (p.186's defining card, and the alphabetical position
!     of KCBJ in the typeset C22-6728 index).  The landed value
!     221313.40 is what this page's SIC prints.
!
! (7) THE BYTE ON LINE 51 IS "A0", NOT "AC".  At 300 dpi it reads
!     AC; at 1200 dpi it is A0, and strap_asm's TI encoder agrees
!     (I2 = 0, no index on the second operand).  An "AC" would
!     mean "JNEWXR($12)" and the statement prints no such index.
!     This one is recorded because the 300-dpi reading was wrong
!     and only the render caught it.
!
! (8) THE NAME-FIELD BLANKS ARE NOT CONSISTENT, ON ONE PAGE.
!     Line 27 prints "J SEOP T" with two blanks; line 34 prints
!     "JSEOPZ" closed up, four characters of which are the same
!     four.  Line 43 prints "JKCCW" closed up, line 51 "JNEWTE"
!     closed up, lines 8 and 15 "JBSPX"/"JBSPC" closed up.
!     strap_asm cannot carry a blank in a label field at all
!     (brief's known-gaps list), so JSEOPT is written closed up.
!     This is a second instance of printed p.184's open note (B)
!     and it still settles nothing about STRAP's own name field.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ELEVEN.  SIX ARE ALREADY LANDED in decks/ and are written in the
! form the landed decks use, so the merged image cannot disagree:
!
!   SREJ     3406.0       landed; this page's LVI prints 003406.35
!   SDISIC   217451.40    landed (pp.103,119,169,173)
!   SDISP    217372.0     landed; NOT the bare-dot spelling, which
!                         the body-image docstring records being
!                         classified as a competing DEFINE
!   KSOS     221274.0     landed
!   KREP     30, (BU,18)  landed; the dds comes from printed
!                         p.185's defining card -- see the note
!   KCBJR    221313.40    landed (pp.125,126,184)
!   KCLEAR   221302.40    landed (pp.125,126,184)
!
! FIVE ARE NEW and every value is READ OFF THIS PAGE'S OWN BINARY
! OUTPUT.  Which are bit-exact and which are not is recorded here
! rather than left to a passing !CHECK:
!
! >>> BIT-EXACT FROM THIS PAGE (the operand is a SIC) <<<
!   KKRET    221512.40    line 1 SIC -- AND printed p.191's OCR
!                         carries its DEFINING card, "221512.40
!                         K K RET BZCBJZ,$", at that location, and
!                         three later pages print "SIC,KKRET"
!                         compiling the same 221512.40 80
!   SDISIC   217451.40    lines 12, 32 SIC (agrees with the landed
!                         value, so this is a real check of it)
!   KCBJR    221313.40    line 37 SIC (ditto)
!
! >>> HALF WORD ONLY (a branch or an index operation; the bit
! >>> within the half word is UNOBSERVABLE, workflow item 1) <<<
!   KIOREJ   221505.0     line  2 B     -> prints 221505.10
!   JBSPE    221514.0     line 10 CB    -> prints 221514.72
!   SREJ       3406.0     lines 11,31 LVI -> prints 003406.35
!   SDISP    217372.0     lines 13,33 B -> prints 217372.10
!   KSOS     221274.0     line  9 BZB   -> prints 221274.34
!   KCLEAR   221302.40    line 38 B     -> prints 221302.50
!   JNEWXR   221617.0     line 51 TI    -> prints 221617.06
!
! For each of these the ".0" is this corpus's CONVENTION and not a
! reading.  Bit 32 IS checked (it is the top bit of the printed
! octal pair), so a symbol really at .40 written .0 would fail --
! KCLEAR's .40 is read that way and so is KKRET's and KCBJR's.
!
! THREE OF THE SEVEN ARE PINNED TO THE BIT BY ANOTHER PAGE, and
! the deck still writes ".0" because a later page's rendering must
! replace an OCR, not be replaced by it.  Recorded so the next
! transcriber does not re-derive them:
!   KIOREJ   printed p.191's OCR line 21 is the DEFINING card,
!            "221505.00  000036.03 02  K IO REJ  LCI,1,K REP",
!            so the bit really is 0.
!   JBSPE    printed p.191's OCR ends at 221514.40, so its line 47
!            is at 221514.00 -- see (B).  A LATER page's OCR also
!            prints "221645.40  221514.10 00  B,JBSPE".
!   JNEWXR   a later page's OCR carries its DEFINING card,
!            "221617.00  000003.60 ...  JNEWXR  DRZ(..),(3)" -- a
!            THREE-WORD RESERVATION, which is also why nothing on
!            this page or the next few can define 221617.
!
! >>> K REP's DATA DESCRIPTION: THE HAZARD WAS REAL AND IT FIRED
! >>> WHILE THIS PAGE WAS BEING WRITTEN. <<<  Worth the space,
! because the sequence is the brief's rule 1 happening live.
!
! The volume OCR carries the defining card -- "K REP SYN(BU,18),30
! -NO GOF I/O RETRIES FOR EKJ", an eighteen-bit unsigned datum --
! and an EARLIER draft of this deck wrote "KREP SYN, 30" WITHOUT
! the dds, to match decks/mcp_bootstrap_p125.strap, which is the
! only other landed deck that mentions KREP.  That draft merged
! green.
!
! It then STOPPED merging, with no change to this deck:
!
!   FAIL KREP is declared with more than one data description:
!        (no dds) on printed p.192; (BU,18) on printed p.125
!
! because printed p.185 landed in the same session, PRINTS the
! defining card at its line 27, and its transcriber corrected
! p.125 to "KREP SYN(BU,18), 30".  This deck now carries the dds
! too and merges again.
!
! TWO THINGS WORTH KEEPING FROM THAT:
!   * the dds CANNOT be seen from this page.  Measured:
!     "LCI,14,K REP" compiles 000036.35 02 with the dds and
!     000036.35 02 without it, because LCI takes the VALUE.  The
!     merge refusal is the ONLY test of the length, exactly as
!     p.125's own note now says.
!   * "match the landed form" is the WRONG rule when the landed
!     form is the one that is wrong.  The right rule is the
!     brief's: the page that PRINTS the definition is the
!     authority, and here the OCR had been pointing at that
!     authority all along.
!
! >>> JKCCW IS BIT-EXACT AND IT IS NOT A CONVENTION. <<<  It is
! defined on this page, and three same-page rows read it:
!   * its own LOCATION column, line 43, prints 221540.00;
!   * line 34's "BB,JKCCW+.24" prints 221540.30 -- BB's first
!     operand is a 24-BIT BIT ADDRESS, so +24 bits -> .30 octal
!     is a reading to the bit;
!   * lines 35 and 39's "L(BU,4),JKCCW+.19" print 221540.23 --
!     a VFL OPERAND, which the workflow's measurement says carries
!     every bit; +19 bits -> .23 octal.
! Three rows, two instruction classes, one answer.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (A) >>> TWO NAMES DEFINED HERE REST ON THIS PAGE'S INK AND ON
!     NOTHING ELSE: JSEOPZ (line 34) and JKCCW (line 43). <<<
!     Both appear in the volume OCR and both appear ONLY in the
!     OCR OF THIS PAGE (PDF p.199) -- the same ink read by a worse
!     reader, which the workflow says is worthless as
!     corroboration.  Counted with WHOLE names, not substrings
!     (brief: `grep -c ZIO` nearly rewrote two correct decks):
!
!       grep -ho 'JSEOPZ[A-Z0-9]*' both volumes -> 1, this page
!       grep -ho 'JKCCW[A-Z0-9]*'               -> 2 JKCCW +
!                                                  1 JKCCWH, all
!                                                  this page
!
!     The other four labels this page defines DO have an
!     other-page witness and are therefore in better shape:
!       JBSPX   a later page's OCR prints "221645.00 221520.40 80
!               J R ACKT SIC,JBSPX -BSP THE TAPE" -- a SIC, so it
!               reads 221520.40 TO THE BIT, from another page
!       JBSPC   printed p.191's OCR line 48 prints a located row
!               at 221514.40 whose half word is "221524.00 10",
!               i.e. this page's JBSPC.  THE MNEMONIC IS NOT
!               NAMED here -- see THE JOIN
!       JSEOPT  a later page's OCR prints "221655.00 221525.10 00
!               B,JSEOPT"
!       JNEWTE  a later page's OCR prints "221663.40 221541.10 00
!               B,JNEWTE" -- which independently pins THIS PAGE'S
!               LAST LOCATION at 221541.00
!     WHAT WOULD SETTLE THE TWO THAT REMAIN: any page referencing
!     221531.00 or 221540.00.  Neither is likely: both are
!     internal to this routine's own loop.
!
! (B) >>> "JBSPE" (line 10): THE ADDRESS IS NOW SETTLED FROM
!     ANOTHER PAGE; THE SPELLING IS NOT. <<<  This page defines
!     JBSPX (line 8) and JBSPC (line 15) but NOT JBSPE, and the
!     three differ only in their last character -- X, C, E --
!     which is exactly the shape of a drum error.  Against that:
!     the three compile to three DIFFERENT addresses (221520.40,
!     221524.00, 221514.00), so they cannot be one symbol
!     misread; the E is a clean E at 600 dpi with no round glyph
!     near it; printed p.191's OCR prints the pair as a LINKAGE
!     comment, "SIC,JBSPX / B,JBSPE", with both spellings on
!     adjacent cards; and a later page's OCR prints the same pair
!     again at 221645.00/221645.40, compiling 221520.40 and
!     221514.10.  So three pages agree that X and E are different
!     characters of the same family.
!     >>> PREDICTION FOR printed p.191: its LAST line is line 48
!     at 221514.40 and it DEFINES a label at 221514.00 whose name
!     this page spells JBSPE. <<<  That is read off p.191's OCR
!     (lines 44-48 above), which is an index and not a rendering;
!     p.191's transcriber should confirm or kill it.
!
! (C) THE SECOND LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK (lines 13 and 41).  This
!     page refutes a statement-based rule from its own ink (see
!     LISTING MARKS) and proposes nothing in its place.
!
! (D) WHETHER "J SEOP T"'s BLANKS ARE DATA (glyph call 8).  Not
!     answerable from here; strap_asm cannot represent the
!     question.
!
! (E) THE BRIEF'S OPEN QUESTION -- does a mode-only dds "(BU)"
!     inherit a LENGTH from its operand symbol? -- IS NOT TOUCHED
!     BY THIS PAGE.  Every dds on the page is "(BU,4)" (lines 35,
!     39), both with an explicit length, and there is no mode-only
!     dds anywhere on it.
!
! (F) K REP's dds is NO LONGER OPEN -- printed p.185 landed
!     mid-session and settled it (BU,18); see EXTERNALS.  What is
!     open is the SHAPE of the problem: a symbol SYNned by three
!     decks whose length only the merge can see, where "match the
!     landed form" and "match the printed definition" gave
!     opposite answers for about an hour.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! JOINING IT TO THE BODY IMAGE -- MEASURED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The join is tests/check_mcp_body_image.py's "FIRST, LAST" and its
! body_page_count, NOT strap/mcp_image.py's MCP_IPL_PAGES.  This
! deck may not edit under tests/, so the merge was run by hand:
!
!   pp.99-184 + this page  ->  merges with NO disagreement,
!                              772 defined, 71 external,
!                              image 0o215000..0o221541, 2156 words
!   origin shifted to (8)221515.40 and re-merged -> ALSO ACCEPTED,
!     772 defined, 71 external -- which is the measurement behind
!     "ASSERTED, not checked" above: no landed deck references any
!     label this page defines.
!
! tests/check_symbol_spellings.py and
! tests/check_deck_listing_comments.py were run the same way,
! against a mirror of the whole landed decks/ directory with this
! deck added -- 1541 symbol definitions, no symbol spelled two
! ways; 118/173 decks with a parseable listing block, 4197 rows
! parsed, 3089 checks compared, 0 mismatches.  Run against this
! deck ALONE the listing-block check compares 32 of 32 rows, so
! the block and the !CHECKs below agree row for row.
!
! >>> AND THE GREEN IS NOT EVIDENCE THAT NOTHING IS MISSING. <<<
! This deck's SLC is a FORWARD SLC over everything pp.185-191 will
! fill, so strap_asm records a skip, and the span was PRINTED from
! the merged build rather than computed by hand:
!
!   skip at word 0o221261, count 0o234 = 156 words
!   i.e. 0o221261..0o221514 inclusive
!
! 0o221261 is exactly where printed p.184 leaves its counter and
! 0o221515 is exactly where this page starts, so the 156 words are
! pp.185-191's and nothing else.  Those seven pages are IN FLIGHT
! as this deck is written; the body image will stay green across a
! gap it should not be green across until they land.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ASSEMBLER: NOTHING REFUSED.  All THIRTY-THREE statements on the
! page (the thirty-two that emit, plus line 14's CNOP, which does
! not) were handed to strap_asm IN THEIR PRINTED FORM and
! accepted -- including the six-letter indicator branch "BZEKJZ",
! the "(SEOP)" modifier with a control code written as an address
! ("(8)176.0"), the bare-decimal bit offsets ".32"/".60"/".61",
! the bare index numbers of "LCI,14,K REP" and "TI,3,$1,JNEWXR",
! the blanked external names "K SOS" and "K REP", and -- tested
! specifically because the brief warns about names inside
! expressions -- LINE 39'S "JKCCW.19" WITH NO PLUS SIGN, which is
! accepted and compiles identically to line 35's "JKCCW+.19".
! The only departure from the page is the NAME-field blank of
! "J SEOP T" (glyph call 8), which strap_asm cannot represent.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

KKRET   SYN, (8)221512.40            ! line  1 SIC -- BIT-EXACT
KIOREJ  SYN, (8)221505.0             ! line  2 B; bit offset unobservable
JBSPE   SYN, (8)221514.0             ! line 10 CB; bit offset unobservable; see (B)
SREJ    SYN, (8)3406.0               ! landed; lines 11/31 print 003406.35
SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40            ! landed pp.103/119/169/173; lines 12/32 SIC -- BIT-EXACT
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0             ! landed; lines 13/33 print 217372.10
KSOS    SYN, (8)221274.0             ! landed; line 9 BZB prints 221274.34
KREP    SYN(BU,18), 30               ! landed; dds from printed p.185's defining card -- see EXTERNALS
KCBJR   SYN, (8)221313.40            ! landed pp.125/126/184; line 37 SIC -- BIT-EXACT
KCLEAR  SYN, (8)221302.40            ! landed pp.125/126/184; line 38 B prints 221302.50
JNEWXR  SYN, (8)221617.0             ! line 51 TI prints 221617.06; bit offset unobservable

        SLC, (8)221515.0             ! NOT PRINTED.  Asserted; see THE JOIN
        SIC,KKRET                    ! line  1   -TO REJECT ROUTINE
        B,KIOREJ                     ! line  2
        LVI,$1,$+1.0                 ! line  3   -TO SEOP TEST
        B,JSEOPT                     ! line  4
        B,JBSPX                      ! line  5   -EPGK IF AT LOAD POINT
        B,JBSPX+.32                  ! line  6   -UK NOT ACCEPTABLE
        NOP                          ! line  7   -EE OK
JBSPX   B,$                          ! line  8   -NORMAL EXIT
        BZB,$R+0.63,K SOS            ! line  9   -BR. IF UK ALONE TO SETUP ERR
        CB,$13,JBSPE+.32             ! line 10   -REISSUE IF UK ALONE
        LVI,$14,SREJ                 ! line 11
        SIC,SDISIC                   ! line 12   -TO ERROR CONTROL
        B,SDISP                      ! line 13 * location-column asterisk
        CNOP                         ! line 14   emits NOTHING here; no location printed
JBSPC   CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),(8)176.0  ! line 15   -BSP COMMAND
! lines 16-26 are comment cards: the banner, and the calling
! sequence of the routine that starts at line 27.
JSEOPT  LCI,14,K REP                 ! line 27   printed name "J SEOP T"
        CCW,0.0($14),JKCCW           ! line 28
        BZEKJZ,JSEOPZ                ! line 29
        CB,$14,JSEOPT+.32            ! line 30
        LVI,$14,SREJ                 ! line 31   -IF EXCHANGE BAD
        SIC,SDISIC                   ! line 32
        B,SDISP                      ! line 33
JSEOPZ  BB,JKCCW+.24,JSEOPT          ! line 34   -LOOP ON SEOP BIT UNTIL I/O IS DONE
        L(BU,4),JKCCW+.19            ! line 35   -EPGK,UK,EE,EOP BITS
        BRZ,1.32($1)                 ! line 36   -NEVER HAVE EOP ALONE
        SIC,KCBJR                    ! line 37   -RELEASE
        B,KCLEAR                     ! line 38   -THE CHANNEL
        L(BU,4),JKCCW.19             ! line 39   PRINTED WITHOUT THE PLUS SIGN
        BB,$R+.60,0.0($1)            ! line 40   -IF EPGK
        BB,$R+.61,.32($1)            ! line 41 * location-column asterisk; -IF UK
        B,1.0($1)                    ! line 42   -MUST BE EE OR EE,EOP
JKCCW   CW,0                         ! line 43   -COPIED CW
! lines 44-50 are comment cards: "***** TRY TO GET A NEW TAPE
! *****" and the linkage SIC,JNEWT / B,JNEWTE.  JNEWT is named
! ONLY in that comment and is therefore NOT a symbol of this deck.
JNEWTE  TI,3,$1,JNEWXR               ! line 51

